From ca36493b87dd8e64a337d44f51a4e40619890692 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:48:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/40] arm64: dts: qcom: Add Nubia RedMagic 11 Pro

Add initial support for the Nubia RedMagic 11 Pro (NX809J), based on the
Kaanapali QRD board file. Working so far:

- Boot with the bootloader framebuffer (simple-framebuffer at the
  cont-splash region)
- UFS storage
- USB in peripheral mode (role switching forced until pmic-glink role
  handling is wired up)
- SoCCP (attached) and ADSP, battery and charger via pmic-glink
- cpufreq via SCMI
- Volume keys, ramoops at the downstream location

Board specifics taken from the downstream device tree: reserved GPIOs,
regulator ranges that differ from QRD, the 70 MiB ADSP carve-out.

The stock ABL only boots this with a shim in front of the kernel, as it
passes the downstream DTB from vendor_boot instead of the appended one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
